From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: drain pipeline cache writes before shutdown

Runtime pipeline entries are appended by VkPipelineSerialization. ThreadWorker
stops its jthreads during member destruction and does not promise to execute
queued work after stop is requested. Drain that queue while PipelineCache is
still alive so vulkan.bin and vulkan_mesh.bin contain the pipelines built in
the session that is closing.

Break risk: shutdown now waits for pending cache serialization. If a cache
write or its filesystem operation stalls, closing the game can take longer;
it must not be enabled if shutdown latency is more important than retaining
that session's cache. This does not change pipeline construction or draw
state, so a bad write is visible as a longer close or as the next launch
rebuilding a pipeline, not as a different rendered frame. The win is a
source-level correctness fix; no PS5 timing measurement is available here.

---
 src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
@@ -827,4 +827,6 @@
 PipelineCache::~PipelineCache() {
+    // Drain queued environment-cache writes before ThreadWorker destruction stops the serializer.
+    serialization_thread.WaitForRequests();
     SaveUsedPipelines();
     if (use_vulkan_pipeline_cache && !vulkan_pipeline_cache_filename.empty()) {
         SerializeVulkanPipelineCache(vulkan_pipeline_cache_filename, vulkan_pipeline_cache,
